\description{
A ready-to-fit sample of the US Forest Inventory and Analysis (FIA) network
in Oregon: 200 training sites (\verb{fia_*_dt} / \code{fia_init_trees}) and 200
disjoint holdout sites (\verb{fia_*_test}) that are never seen during fitting, so
a model fit on the training tables can be scored genuinely out of sample.
The tables are already in FINN's input format -- IDs resolved, species
re-indexed \verb{1..K} -- so they go straight into \code{\link[=fit]{fit()}} / \code{\link[=simulateForest]{simulateForest()}}
without \code{\link[=makeObsData]{makeObsData()}} or \code{\link[=resolveSiteIDs]{resolveSiteIDs()}}. The \code{D-Fit_to_FIA} and
\code{E-Mortality} vignettes are the worked examples.
}
